:: Mansion Bank Account Notice
<<set $hbsc.averyAccountUnlockPending to false>><<set $hbsc.averyAccountUnlockNoticeSeen to true>>
Avery stands on the mansion steps with one gloved hand resting on the rail, posture relaxed, expression calm.
<<He>> looks perfectly put together, like <<he>> wanted to make an impression.
<br><br>
<<He>> was expecting you. You walk closer.
<br><br>
"HBSC..." <<His>> gaze drifts over your face, then your pocket, then back again. "You opened an account."
<br><br>
"How do you even know that?" you ask.
<br><br>
"Clerks gossip. Managers posture. Servants listen. There are always people desperate to be the first to bring me
something they think I ought to know." Avery gives the faintest smile. "And when <i>you</i> do something faintly ambitious,
it reaches my ears faster than most."
<br><br>
Avery says the last part casually, but there's a clear purpose behind it. <<He>> didn't stop you on the steps just to chat.
"Come inside. If you've attached yourself to something respectable, then you may as well learn why it matters."
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Avery.love gte 60>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Bank Account Notice - Drink Offered]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Bank Account Notice - Ordered to Serve]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Bank Account Notice - Drink Offered
The sitting room is already warm when you enter, firelight shining over the polished wood and crystal.
Avery gestures for you to sit, then walks calmly to the drinks cabinet.
<br><br>
"You look tense. Try not to make a vulgar occasion of this."
<<He>> pours two drinks, then brings one over and places it in your hand himself. The glass is cool; <<his>> fingers are not.
<br><br>
"You've done something moderately civilised. It would be a shame to greet it like a panicked child with loose coins in their fist."
Avery settles opposite you, one leg crossing over the other. <<His>> eyes never quite leave your face. There is approval there.
<br><br>
"Drink," <<he>> says. "And listen."
<br><br>
<<if playerIsPregnant() and playerAwareTheyArePregnant()>>
	<span class="blue">You can't bring yourself to drink while you know you're with child.</span>
	<br>
	<<link [[Listen|Mansion Bank Account Notice - The Owner]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Drink and listen|Mansion Bank Account Notice - The Owner]]>><<alcohol 200>><</link>><<ggalcohol>>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Bank Account Notice - Ordered to Serve
Avery leads you into one of the sitting rooms and stops beside the drinks trolley.
"Pour for me," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
You reach for the bottle while <<he>> watches you closely. Even pouring a drink feels like a test.
"Careful," <<he>> says as the drink splashes into the crystal glass.
"If you're going to try banking, do try not to start by staining my carpet."
<br><br>
When the glass is filled, you hand it over. Avery takes it without thanks and only then gestures toward a seat for you.
"You may as well hear this properly," <<he>> says, settling back. "Since you've involved yourself in the matter already."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Bank Account Notice - The Owner]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Bank Account Notice - The Owner
<<effects>>
For a moment Avery simply turns the glass in <<his>> hand, watching the amber slide against the cut crystal.
<br><br>
"<span class="elk">The owner</span>," <<he>> says at last, "is not someone to play around with."
<br><br>
That gets your full attention. Avery notices, and seems faintly pleased by it.
<br><br>
"No, I don't know who they are," <<he>> continues before you can ask. "Not properly.
I don't know whether they're in this city at all. Some people swear they are.
Others speak as if the entire enterprise runs itself by reputation alone."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Bank Account Notice - The Owner 2]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Bank Account Notice - The Owner 2
<<effects>>
Avery lifts <<his>> drink. "But you can still feel their influence. Everyone knows about them.
<span class="lewd">Those pills.</span> And now a bank. Everyone knows it matters.
But respectable people do not gossip about the owner as if they know them personally. That would be terribly vulgar.
They speak carefully instead, pretending their curiosity is not there."
<br><br>
<<if $remy_name_known is true or $remysurname is true or $remyinit is true>>
	"Even Remy is careful about it. And Remy does not enjoy sounding careful."
<</if>>
<<He>> adds, "That alone tells me enough. Whoever is behind HBSC must matter, if important people are careful about how they speak of them."
<br><br>
<<He>> leans back, eyes half-lidded. "Do you understand how rare that is? Everyone knows them, almost no one talks about them,
and still they are treated with respect. People like you ask ordinary questions. People like me notice what people refuse to say."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Bank Account Notice - Avery's Interest]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Bank Account Notice - Avery's Interest
"So," Avery says, looking at you over the rim of <<his>> glass, "opening an account there is not just about having somewhere to keep your money.
It gives you a touch of respectability. Perhaps even opportunity."
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Avery.rage gte 60>>
	A faint smile appears. "Do not flatter yourself. This does not make you my rival.
	It only means you might be useful. If that bank ever matters to me, your little account may come in handy."
	<br><br>
	<<if C.npc.Avery.love gte 60>>
		<<He>> studies you. "You are useful to me more often than not. I would rather you learnt how to behave in better company without embarrassing me."
	<<else>>
		"Try not to mistake access for status," <<he>> adds. "A bank card does not make you important. You are still ordinary, replaceable, and easy to put back in your place."
	<</if>>
<<elseif C.npc.Avery.rage lt 20 and C.npc.Avery.love gte 60>>
	Avery smiles to <<himself>>. "You don't grab at that kind of influence. You approach it carefully, and with grace."
	<<He>> looks back at you. "Being allowed close to something like that... yes. I can see why it appeals."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> taps a finger once against the glass. "And for once, you've found something with real polish. I'm proud of you. Truly. You can be quite impressive when it matters."
<<elseif C.npc.Avery.rage lt 20>>
	Avery inclines <<his>> head. "At the very least, it gives you practice in looking less out of place.
	I do not need you acting like some dull little banker. I need you paying attention.
	If the bank ever becomes useful to me, I would rather have someone there already than start from nothing."
<<else>>
	"You may ignore all this," Avery says, "and carry on playing the ordinary little banker, pleased with ledgers and tidy accounts. Dull, but not surprising."
	<br><br>
	"Or perhaps you are sensible enough to realise that places like this can be useful, if you know how to use them.
	I have not spent my life standing at doors. I prefer opening them.
	<<if C.npc.Avery.love gte 60>>
	And if this leads anywhere useful," <<he>> adds, "I would rather have you nearby when I find out."
	<<else>>
	If you can be useful in this, I will find out before you do," <<he>> says. "Count on that."
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
Avery sets <<his>> glass aside with care. "So keep the account. Learn the routine. Listen more than you speak. And if you hear anything unusual, you will tell me."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Bank Account Notice - Conclusion]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Bank Account Notice - Conclusion
Avery rises. "Now you see why I stopped you on the steps, rather than letting you stroll in here with that card and your smug little pride."
<<if C.npc.Avery.love gte 60>>
	<<He>> pauses close to you, lightly straightening your sleeve. "You've done well. Don't spoil it by acting common."
<<else>>
	<<He>> glances once toward the door. "Try not to make me regret the time I've spent explaining this to you."
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Make proper use of it," Avery says. "Don't just sit there admiring it."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Garden]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress Ask
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
	"I don't mean to question you," you say, "but why me?"
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Why am I the one being paraded around?" you ask.
<<else>>
	"Why do I need to be there?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Avery smooths a cufflink. "Charity is theatre. Banking is theatre. And tonight I'd rather have you on my arm than the usual parade of simpering heirs and brittle wives."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks you over. "<span class="elk">HBSC's owner</span> doesn't attend, of course. People like that rarely need to be seen. Their influence is enough. The branch manager, the trustees, the donors, the families trying to impress one another... all of them will be there instead. And so will you.
You'll smile, stand where you're useful, and help improve the image of my household. With luck, you'll even learn something."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress Revealing
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
	"I'd rather wear something a little more daring for you," you say.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"This is too stiff," you say. "Give me something worth looking at."
<<else>>
	"I'd like something more revealing," you say.
<</if>>
<<exhibitionism1>>
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Avery.rage gte random(20, 100) and $averyragerevealed gte 1>>
	"You'll wear what I tell you to wear," Avery says. "This isn't a brothel, it's a bank gala. Get dressed properly."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress 2]]>>
		<<if $player.gender_appearance is "m">>
			<<upperwear "tuxedo jacket">>
			<<lowerwear "tuxedo trousers">>
		<<else>>
			<<upperwear "evening gown">>
		<</if>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	Avery considers you for a long moment. "Tempting," <<he>> says. "But there are degrees of indecency. Tonight we use the expensive sort."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> searches the wardrobe and produces
	<<if $player.gender_appearance is "m">>
		a velvet dinner jacket with fitted trousers,
		<<upperwear "double breasted jacket">>
		<<lowerwear "breeches">>
	<<else>>
		a short ballgown,
		<<upperwear "short ballgown">>
	<</if>>
	then steps aside to let you change.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress 2]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress Class
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
	"Could I have something finer?" you ask.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"If I'm going to represent you, I should look expensive," you say.
<<else>>
	"Can I have something finer?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Avery.rage gte random(20, 100) and $averyragerevealed gte 1>>
	"You should look obedient," Avery says. "Don't confuse the two."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress 2]]>>
		<<if $player.gender_appearance is "m">>
			<<upperwear "tuxedo jacket">>
			<<lowerwear "tuxedo trousers">>
		<<else>>
			<<upperwear "evening gown">>
		<</if>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	Avery's mouth curves. "A sensible instinct. Fine things invite better assumptions."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> chooses another outfit,
	<<if $player.gender_appearance is "m">>
		a peacoat with suit trousers,
		<<upperwear "peacoat">>
		<<lowerwear "suit trousers">>
	<<else>>
		a full ballgown,
		<<upperwear "ballgown">>
	<</if>>
	and leaves you to dress.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress 2]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress 2
<<effects>>
You finish dressing and step outside. Avery is waiting for you, one hand resting on <<his>> cane, gaze moving over you in a slow, assessing sweep.
<br><br>
"Acceptable," <<he>> says at last.
<br><br>
The journey to the bank passes in silence. By the time the car stops, servants are already opening doors beneath HBSC's polished facade. A gilded banner reads <i>Annual Charity Gala</i> in letters meant to be admired, not read. You follow Avery through the branch and up a private staircase, away from the counters and into a softly lit salon built for money to flatter itself.
<br><br>
Crystal chandeliers gleam above white tablecloths and discreet floral arrangements. A string quartet plays near the windows. Beyond them, the city glows.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Arrival]]>><<pass 30>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress Refuse
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
	"I don't want to go," you say quietly.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"I'm not dressing up so you can show me off to bankers," you say.
<<else>>
	"I'm not in the mood for this," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Avery.rage gte random(20, 100) and $averyragerevealed gte 1>>
	Avery's expression hardens. "You are not being consulted." <<He>> catches your arm before you can step back. "I'm not arriving alone because you suddenly remembered how to sulk."<<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 4>><<stress 4>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Go with Avery (0:05)|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress Angry]]>><<endevent>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Fight|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress Fight]]>><<set $fightstart to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	Avery exhales through <<his>> nose. "Then I'll ask once more. Try to be useful, or stay here and waste both our evenings."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Go with Avery (0:05)|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress 2]]>>
		<<pass 5>>
		<<if $player.gender_appearance is "m">>
			<<upperwear "tuxedo jacket">>
			<<lowerwear "tuxedo trousers">>
		<<else>>
			<<upperwear "evening gown">>
		<</if>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Cancel the evening|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Dress Cancel]]>><<npcincr Avery love -3>><</link>><<lllove>>
	<br>
<</if>>

