:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Task Matron
<<effects>><<person2>>
You approach the matron overseeing the scholarship display, a composed older <<person>> with diamonds at <<his>> throat and a memory sharpened by years of sorting generous people from merely rich ones.
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
	You offer a careful greeting, then praise the students being supported this year.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	You flash a practiced smile and ask which scholarship attracts the most competitive donors.
<<else>>
	You introduce yourself politely and ask about the scholarship fund.
<</if>>
<br><br>
The matron warms as <<he>> speaks, pleased to have an attentive audience. By the time you excuse yourself, <<he>> is looking at you as though you might be more than someone's ornament.
<br><br>
Across the room, Avery catches your eye and gives the smallest approving tilt of <<person1>><<his>> chin.
<br><br><<famesocial 5>>
<<run $avery_party.hbsc.tasks.pushUnique("matron")>>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Tasks]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Task Donors
<<effects>>
You drift among the lesser donors clustered around the champagne and auction cards, where the sort of people who speak too softly about sums that could feed streets.
<br><br>
You laugh where appropriate, nod when someone mentions legacy, and let them look you over while deciding whether you're decorative, useful, or being quietly tested on Avery's behalf.
<br><br>
One of them remarks that Avery seems to be cultivating better company lately. It takes you a moment to realise they mean you.
<br><br><<famesocial 5>>
<<run $avery_party.hbsc.tasks.pushUnique("donors")>>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Tasks]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Task Message
<<effects>>
Avery intercepts you to pass along a folded card and a line to memorise.
"To the trustee in green. Tell <<person3>><<him>> that the revised figure is acceptable, but only if the naming rights remain under discussion. Repeat it exactly. If your imagination stirs, kill it."
<br><br>
You do as instructed. The trustee reads the card, studies you for a moment, then gives a slow nod. Whatever currents are moving beneath tonight's polished surface, your message slots neatly.
<br><br>
When you return, Avery's mouth twitches with approval. "See? You can be useful without causing a scene."
<br><br><<famesocial 5>>
<<run $avery_party.hbsc.tasks.pushUnique("message")>>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Tasks]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Murmurs
<<effects>>
On your way back across the salon, a murmur catches your ear from behind a half-closed service door.
"Not on the main floor. The manager wants the ordinary stock displayed, not those."
<br>
"Then keep the anti separate," another voice answers, lower. "You want one of the donors swallowing the wrong thing?"
<br><br>
Something cold settles in your stomach.
<br><br>
A waiter passes with a tray, masking the sound as you edge closer. Through the gap you glimpse two sharply dressed figures and a bank employee in evening black, gathered around a sideboard. Cases lie open atop velvet. One contains pills in familiar colours.
<span class="lewd">X-Change pills.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Get closer|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Investigation]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Step away and ignore it|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Ignore]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Investigation
<<effects>>
You slip into the service corridor and keep to the shadow cast by a column. The voices sharpen.
"The demonstration cases stay sealed. <span class="elk">The owner</span> doesn't want improvisation tonight. The charity is for upstairs. The real clients come later."
<br><br>
One of the strangers opens another velvet box, checks its contents, and sets a single pill case apart from the rest. Even from here, the label catches your eye. It isn't one of the standard transformation pills.
<span class="green">But an anti pill.</span>
<br><br>
/* Brown fox HBSC Gala task: discovering the hidden cache counts as success */
<<if $avery_mansion.fox.task is "HBSC Gala">>
	<<set $avery_mansion.fox.task_complete to "success">>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Investigation 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Investigation 2
<<effects>>
The case sits for one exposed on the corner of the sideboard while the three of them argue over the rest of the stock. 
<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
	But your hands twitch uselessly. <span class="red">You can't steal anything with both arms bound.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back away|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Ignore]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	/* Set skulduggerydifficulty here so the skulduggerydifficulty gauge below reflects THIS steal, not a stale value left over from lockpicking or another skulduggery action. */
	<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 1000>>
	<<if currentSkillValue('skulduggery') gte $skulduggerydifficulty>>
		<span class="green">You could probably lift it before they look back.</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="red">It would take quick, careful fingers to steal it cleanly.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Try to take the anti pill|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Steal]]>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave it and return to the gala|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Ignore]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Steal
<<effects>>
You wait for the smallest opening: one stranger turning to hiss at the other, the employee glancing toward the hall.
<br><br>
/* Use the standard skulduggery check (difficulty 1000) so odds scale smoothly with skill and match the gauge shown on the previous screen. At S rank the gap guaranteeing success; a still-caught path exists for lower skill. */
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 1000>><<skulduggerycheck "silent">>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1 and !pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
	Your hand darts out and back again in one smooth motion. The case disappears into your sleeve before anyone turns.
	<br><br>
	<<set $avery_party.hbsc.pillTaken to true>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Steal Success]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	Your fingers brush the case, but not cleanly enough.
	<br><br>
	"Hey...!"
	<br><br>
	A hand clamps around your wrist. Another seizes your shoulder. The service door swings shut behind you as they drag you out of sight.
	<br><br>
	<<set $avery_party.hbsc.failed to true>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Steal Fail]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Steal Success
<<effects>>
You don't stop until you're down the corridor and shielded by the laughing donors.
<br><br>
Only then do you let yourself breathe. Hidden in your palm is the stolen case, sleek and familiar in a way that quickens your curiosity at once.
<br><br>

/* RNG roll */
<<set _roll to random(1,100)>>
/* Decide which Choice Reversal would be valid/visible for the current PC */
<<set _choiceValid to V.xchange.pill.choiceEffect>>
<<set _choiceKey to "">>
<<if _choiceValid>>
	<<set _choiceKey to (($xchange.pill.originalBody?.sex || $player.sex) is "m") ? "X-Change Choice Reversal (F)" : "X-Change Choice Reversal (M)">>
<</if>>
/* Build SWP Anti pill candidates */
<<set _antiKeys to Object.keys($sexStats.pills["pills"]).filter(k => k.startsWith("SWP Anti-") && k.endsWith(" Pill"))>>
/* Pick the reward */
<<if _choiceValid and _roll lte 25>>
	<<set _giftKey to _choiceKey>>
<<else>>
	<<set _giftKey to (_antiKeys.length gt 0) ? _antiKeys[random(0, _antiKeys.length - 1)] : "X-Change Choice Reversal (F)">>
<</if>>
/* Ensure entry exists */
<<run if (V.sexStats.pills && V.sexStats.pills.pills && V.sexStats.pills.pills[_giftKey] === undefined) V.sexStats.pills.pills[_giftKey] = { autoTake:false, doseTaken:0, owned:0, overdose:0 }; >>
/* Increment owned safely */
<<if $sexStats.pills["pills"][_giftKey].owned is undefined>>
	<<set $sexStats.pills["pills"][_giftKey].owned to 0>>
<</if>>
<<set $sexStats.pills["pills"][_giftKey].owned to $sexStats.pills["pills"][_giftKey].owned + 1>>
<<set $sexStats.pills.boughtOnce to true>>
<<set $avery_party.hbsc.giftKey to _giftKey>>

You open the case just enough to confirm what you've taken. <span class="green">It's the <<= _giftKey>>.</span>
<br><br>
Avery is still across the room, speaking to a trustee.
<br><br>
<<if !$avery_mansion.hbsc_gala_seen>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Success Show]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Success Hide]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Success Show
<<effects>>
<<set $avery_party.hbsc.pillShown to true>><<person1>>
/* TODO: Make raid event using this check: */ <<set $hbsc.galaAntiPillStolen to true>>
You wait until Avery drifts close enough, then shield the case between your hands and let <<him>> see it.
<br><br>
For the first time tonight, <<his>> composure slips. <<His>> gaze drops to the case, then lifts to your face, and the look that passes between you is not surprise. It's recognition. Avery knows what those <span class="lewd">pills</span> are. Avery knows who makes them.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Success Show 2]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Success Show 2
<<effects>><<person1>>
<<if C.npc.Avery.rage gte 60>>
	"You stole that here." Avery takes the case from your hand, studies the label with narrowed eyes, then pushes it back into your grip with controlled force.
	<br><br>
	"Do you understand what you've just done?" <<His>> voice stays low, clipped, but there is something underneath the anger. "<span class="elk">The owner's</span> people were running product through a charity floor. their floor. Under their roof. And you slipped past them like they were nothing."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> glances toward the service corridor. "That means their operation has cracks. Real ones. The sort of cracks that someone with patience and the right leverage might pry open." 
	<br><br>
	<<His>> jaw works once. "I should be furious with you for taking that kind of risk in front of half the donors in this city. But I'm not. Because you've just shown me something nobody else at this gala could.
	Keep it hidden."<<npcincr Avery love 1>><<glove>>
<<elseif C.npc.Avery.love gte 60 and C.npc.Avery.rage lt 20>>
	"Look at you. You walked into <span class="elk">the owner</span>'s bank, past <span class="elk">the owner</span>'s people, lifted one of <span class="elk">the owner</span>'s pills, and came back to me with it like a cat dropping a bird on the doorstep." 
	<br><br>
	Avery's thumb traces the edge of your knuckle, pressing the case shut between your joined hands. "You know what this means, don't you? Not the pill itself, anyone with enough money can get those. It's what the theft proves. Their people had a blind spot. On their own ground, at their own event, and a clever pair of hands walked right through it."
	<br><br>
	<<His>> eyes gleam. "If someone like you can reach that far in, then perhaps <span class="elk">the owner</span> isn't quite so untouchable as everyone pretends. Keep the pill. You've earned it. And you've given me something far more valuable than medicine tonight."<<npcincr Avery love 2>><<gglove>>
<<else>>
	Avery takes one look at the case and goes very still. When <<he>> speaks, it's barely above the noise of the quartet.
	<br><br>
	"You took this from the back rooms." <<He>> turns so that <<his>> body shields you from the rest of the salon. "From <span class="elk">the owner</span>'s people."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> doesn't touch the case. <<He>> doesn't need to. <<He>> knows what's inside. "Everyone in this room will tell you <span class="elk">the owner</span> is untouchable. That their operation runs without a single loose thread. And yet here you are, holding proof that their staff can be beaten by someone who doesn't even own a proper suit."
	<br><br>
	A faint smile crosses <<his>> face. "I was beginning to think tonight would only produce speeches and bad wine. Instead you've shown me something useful: a gap in their armour. Small, perhaps. But real." <<He>> straightens your collar. "Well done."<<npcincr Avery love 1>><<glove>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Good]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Success Hide
<<effects>><<person1>>
You slip the case away and return to Avery with your face arranged into something calm.
"There you are. I was about to decide whether you'd wandered off on purpose or by instinct."
<br><br>
You murmur an apology and resume your place near <<him>>. If Avery notices the tension in your posture, <<he>> says nothing. But more than once, you catch <<him>> watching you with narrowed curiosity.
<br><br>
The rest of the evening passes in a blur of polished voices and expensive restraint.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Quiet]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Steal Fail
<<effects>><<person1>>
They haul you through a side door into a private office lined with ledgers and locked cabinets. The bank employee's pleasant public face is gone. 
<br><br>
One of the strangers twists your arm higher until pain sparks up to your shoulder.
"Thought you were clever? Do you have any idea whose floor you're sneaking around on?"
<br><br>
Before you can answer, the office door opens.
<br><br>
Avery steps in. <<His>> expression could freeze blood. "There you are," <<he>> says, not looking at you first. "I was wondering why my evening had grown quieter."
<br><br>
The bank employee releases you at once. "This one was caught trying to steal from restricted stock."
<br><br>
Avery's gaze drifts to the sideboard, then back to your captors. "How embarrassing. For everyone involved. My companion clearly strayed somewhere <<pshe>> <<pverb "was not" "were not">> meant to. And you, apparently, were keeping the sort of company that requires a locked office at a charity gala."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Steal Fail 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Steal Fail 2
<<effects>><<person1>>
Silence spreads.
<br><br>
"I'm taking <<phim>> off your hands," Avery says. "Unless you'd prefer I repeat that sentence in front of the trustees."
<br><br>
No one stops <<him>> when <<he>> takes hold of your arm roughly and marches you into the corridor.<<pain 4>><<gpain>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Fail Avery]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Fail Avery
<<effects>><<person1>>
Avery doesn't stop until <<he>> has you in a deserted alcove overlooking the banking hall below. The music is muffled here. <<His>> grip bites through your sleeve.<<pain 2>><<gpain>>
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Avery.rage gte 60>>
	"What," <<he>> asks with terrifying softness, "possessed you to humiliate me in a room full of donors?"
	<br><br>
	"You don't get caught stealing from a bank gala and expect me to find it charming. I had to step between you and a very ugly conversation."
	<br><br>
	"You should explain exactly what piece of your brain failed first. But no need, your brain indeed as slow as that." <<He>> leans close. "You will stay at my side for the rest of the evening. You will smile when spoken to."
	<<npcincr Avery rage 3>><<npcincr Avery love -2>><<ggarage>><<lllove>>
<<elseif C.npc.Avery.love gte 60 and C.npc.Avery.rage lt 20>>
	Avery closes <<his>> eyes for one brief, pained second. "You are lucky I noticed you were gone."
	<br><br>
	When <<he>> looks at you again, the anger is tempered by reluctant concern. "If you wanted something, you should have come to me. Instead you chose the one method guaranteed to make me pull you out of trouble by the wrist like an unruly child.
	Don't make me do that again."<<npcincr Avery rage 1>><<npcincr Avery love -1>><<garage>><<llove>>
<<else>>
	Avery's lip curls with terrifying softness. "I bring you here to improve your image, and you vanish into a service corridor to paw at contraband. Do you understand how vulgar that is?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> straightens your clothes with irritated movements. "You will remain visible for the rest of the evening. I refuse to spend another ten minutes wondering which locked room you've disgraced me in."
	<<npcincr Avery rage 2>><<npcincr Avery love -2>><<ggarage>><<lllove>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
You return to the gala under Avery's watchful shadow, acutely aware of every glance that lands on you.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Bad]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Ignore
<<effects>><<person1>>
You let the murmur go. Whatever is happening behind that service door, it isn't something you can touch without risk.
<br><br>
When you return, Avery studies your face as though weighing whether you merely obeyed or chose restraint.
<br><br>
"Back already?" <<he>> asks.
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
	"I thought it wiser not to cause a scene," you say.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"I decided not to snoop in a bank full of rich idiots," you say.
<<else>>
	"I decided not to interfere," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Avery.rage lt 20>>
	Avery gives a small nod. "Good. Discretion is rarer than bravery, and often worth more."
	<<npcincr Avery love 1>><<glove>>
<<elseif C.npc.Avery.rage gte 60>>
	Avery hums. "Prudent. For once."
<<else>>
	"A pity," Avery says. "But perhaps caution is the more respectable look tonight."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Quiet]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala Avery
<<effects>><<person1>>
You return to Avery's side. <<He>> barely turns <<his>> head, but the corner of <<his>> mouth shifts as you fall back into place.
<br><br>
<<if $avery_party.hbsc.tasks.length is 0>>
	"Already?" <<he>> asks. "Go make yourself useful."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Tasks]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $avery_party.hbsc.tasks.length is 1>>
	"One task completed is not a triumph," Avery says. "Try again."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala Tasks]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	Avery lets you remain beside <<him>> through the close of the auction. By the end of it, several guests have smiled at you as though you might someday become tolerable.
	<<if C.npc.Avery.love gte 60 and C.npc.Avery.rage lt 20>>
		"You cleaned up well. I might even bring you to the next one."
		<<npcincr Avery love 1>><<glove>>
	<<elseif C.npc.Avery.rage gte 60>>
		"Adequate. You embarrassed yourself less than usual."
	<<else>>
		"You served your purpose. Which, tonight, is almost praise."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Quiet]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Good
<<effects>><<person1>>
The gala winds down in the usual way with donors satisfied that they've been seen, glasses emptied, and the illusion of public virtue carefully preserved for another time.
<br><br>
Avery leads you back downstairs through the sleeping bank. <<He>> keeps one hand light at the small of your back, proprietary and warm.
<br><br>
<<if !$avery_mansion.hbsc_gala_seen>>
	Near the entrance, a silver-haired <<person4>><<person>> in a charcoal suit steps forward. <<He>> has the bearing of someone used to standing between wealth and a foundation trustee, or something close to it.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> glances at Avery first, then at you. "I don't believe we've been introduced. And you are...?"
	<br><br>
	Avery's hand presses tighter at your back. "Mine," <<person1>><<he>> says. Then, with a fraction more civility: "From the orphanage. But presentable, as you can see."
	<br><br>
	The <<person4>><<person>>'s expression shifts with warm enough to pass for it. "Then you qualify for the foundation's charitable consideration," <<he>> says. <<He>> produces a small card and writes something on it. "We'll transfer <<printmoney `divineTfIncome(300000, "avery")`>> to your HBSC savings. A modest gesture, but the bank's charter insists."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> nods once to Avery and steps aside.
	<br><br>

	/* Charity payout; deposited to HBSC savings, respects tier deposit cap */
	<<set _xferResult to setup.hbsc.receiveExternalDeposit(divineTfIncome(300000, "avery"))>>
	<<if _xferResult.overflow>>
		<span class="red">Your HBSC savings didn't have enough room for the full transfer. The remainder was added to the cash you're carrying.</span>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<set $avery_mansion.hbsc_gala_seen to true>>
<<else>>
	Near the entrance, the same silver-haired <<person4>><<person>> from the foundation is waiting by the door. <<He>> catches your eye and gives a familiar nod.
	"Back again. I'll have the usual transferred to your account." <<He>> inclines <<his>> head toward Avery. "The foundation's compliments, as always."
	<br><br>
	Avery smiles at that.<<npcincr Avery love 1>><<glove>>
	<br><br>

	/* Repeat charity payout; respects tier deposit cap */
	<<set _xferResult to setup.hbsc.receiveExternalDeposit(divineTfIncome(300000, "avery"))>>
	<<if _xferResult.overflow>>
		<span class="red">Your HBSC savings didn't have enough room for the full transfer. The remainder was added to the cash you're carrying.</span>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Good 2]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Good 2
<<effects>><<pass 120>><<set $location to "avery_mansion">>
"A productive evening," Avery says as you step outside. "You looked presentable, followed direction, and came away with something interesting. That's nearly enough to make me indulgent."
<br><br>
"The guest I originally invited has only been delayed," <<he>> adds. "They'll be the guest of honour at the next party."
<br><br>
The car door is held open. The city air hits cooler after the bank's curated warmth as you going back to the mansion.
<br><br><<endevent>>
<<avery_mansion_party_end>>
<<avery_mansion_end_links>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Quiet
<<effects>>
By the time the last applause fades, your feet ache and your face is tired from holding the shape polite company expects.
<br><br>
<<if !$avery_mansion.hbsc_gala_seen>>
	On the way out, a silver-haired <<person4>><<person>> in a charcoal suit intercepts you both. <<He>> looks you over with the kind of professional curiosity that comes from years of sorting donors from decoration.
	<br><br>
	"One moment," <<he>> says. <<He>> turns to Avery. "Your companion... from the orphanage, I'm told?"
	<br><br>
	Avery inclines <<person1>><<his>> head. The <<person4>><<person>> nods, produces a card, and scratches some numbers on it. "The foundation extends its charitable consideration. <<printmoney `divineTfIncome(300000, "avery")`>> will be transferred to their HBSC savings." <<He>> tucks the card into <<his>> breast pocket. "Good evening to you both."
	<br><br>

	/* Charity payout; deposited to HBSC savings, respects tier deposit cap */
	<<set _xferResult to setup.hbsc.receiveExternalDeposit(divineTfIncome(300000, "avery"))>>
	<<if _xferResult.overflow>>
		<span class="red">Your HBSC savings didn't have enough room for the full transfer. The remainder was added to the cash you're carrying.</span>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<set $avery_mansion.hbsc_gala_seen to true>>
<<else>>
	The silver-haired <<person4>><<person>> from the foundation catches you near the exit. "The usual <<printmoney `divineTfIncome(300000, "avery")`>>," <<he>> says with a brief nod. "Do come again."
	<br><br>

	/* Repeat charity payout; respects tier deposit cap */
	<<set _xferResult to setup.hbsc.receiveExternalDeposit(divineTfIncome(300000, "avery"))>>
	<<if _xferResult.overflow>>
		<span class="red">Your HBSC savings didn't have enough room for the full transfer. The remainder was added to the cash you're carrying.</span>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Quiet 2]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Quiet 2
<<effects>><<pass 120>><<set $location to "avery_mansion">>
<<person1>>Avery escorts you into the night with measured satisfaction. "Not perfect," <<he>> says. "But no disasters. In this city, that puts you ahead of most people with money."
<br><br>
"The guest I originally invited has only been delayed," <<he>> adds. "They'll be the guest of honour at the next party."
<br><br>
You leave the bank beneath discreet lights and thoughts heavier than when you arrived at the mansion.
<br><br><<endevent>>
<<avery_mansion_party_end>>
<<avery_mansion_end_links>>

:: Mansion Party HBSC Gala End Bad
<<effects>><<pass 120>><<set $location to "avery_mansion">>
The gala limps to its conclusion under Avery's iron attention. You remain close, speak only when expected, and feel every second pressing against your skin.
<br><br>
When you finally leave, Avery does not offer <<his>> arm.
"You will be useful to me again," <<he>> says as the car door shuts. "See that next time you remember the difference between initiative and stupidity."
<br><br>
"The guest I originally invited has only been delayed. They'll be the guest of honour at the next party. Do not embarrass me twice."
<br><br>
The ride back to the mansion feels much longer than the journey there.
<br><br><<endevent>>
<<avery_mansion_party_end>>
<<avery_mansion_end_links>>
